## Section & Document Detection

### The State Machine

```

SECTION TRACKING STATE MACHINE

State: IDLE

  Trigger: Markdown header detected (# ## ###)

  Transition → IN_SECTION

State: IN_SECTION

  Trigger: Another header of same/higher level

  Transition → NEW_SECTION (close current, start new)



  Trigger: Header of lower level (e.g., ### after ##)

  Transition → IN_SUBSECTION (nest under current)



  Trigger: Formatting pattern breaks (no header for N paragraphs)

  Transition → DOCUMENT_BREAK or IDLE

State: DOCUMENT_BREAK

  Trigger: New formatting pattern starts

  Transition → IN_SECTION (new document)

CROSS-CHUNK CONTINUATION:

  Chunk N ends with: "## Introduction\n\nThis is the..."

  Chunk N+1 starts with: "...continuation of intro.\n\n## Methods"



  State carries: section_id, section_level, formatting_pattern

  Chunk N+1 receives: continuation context



